---
name: multi-view-reference
description: Make requested front, side, back or three-quarter pixel-art views from an accepted character identity. Preserve proportions, outfit and palette roles, and disclose invented hidden details; do not redesign the character independently for each angle.
---

# Multi-view Reference

Read `references/runtime.md` before using tools or scripts. Derive the requested angles from one accepted identity; views are reference evidence, not another design competition.

## Choose the scope and identity

Read `references/project-contract.md` and inspect the accepted identity and native study. Obtain missing identity acceptance or route to `character-identity`; ask only for blocking choices.
- **Standalone view or view set:** Use the compact record/helper contract in `references/standalone-records.md`. Retain `project.json`/`profile.json` for pipeline helpers without requiring a full run directory or portable bundle.
- **Requested multi-stage workflow, cross-session continuation or portable handoff:** Read `references/run-records.md` and `references/portable-handoff.md`. Check the supplied bundle, inspect its assets and continue its approval scope, records and remaining budget. Reconstruct context from those artifacts, not hidden history.

Record requested angles, character-left/right versus viewer-left/right, native canvas, head/body scale, root/ground anchor, proportions, outfit, palette roles and silhouette features. Reuse an accepted angle when suitable; one requested view does not imply a full turnaround. Set bounded calls/repairs before generation. All attempts, including failed/cancelled/pending starts, count across stages and sessions.

## Derive, compare, accept

1. Record exact prompt, tool arguments and reference roles/hashes before each imagegen call. Use accepted identity as primary reference and relevant accepted neighboring views as support, never the last generated view alone. When an accepted native identity/master exists, inspect and use its exact integer nearest-neighbor enlargement as the primary pixel reference; large concepts are supplementary.
2. Generate missing views separately, preserving proportions, outfit, materials, palette roles and projection. Change only the view relationship. Name visible/hidden features; do not blindly mirror asymmetric details or reverse handedness.
3. Preserve every returned original unchanged in a unique attempt path and retain rejected candidates. Measure actual source geometry before `prepare_pixels.sh --project project.json`; see `references/pixel-tooling.md`. Do not per-view trim/recenter, stretch a wrong aspect or assume a grid lock matches because requested sizes match.
4. Review each native study at 1× and enlargement beside identity and earlier views. Check face/species, body and limb proportions, accessory side, garment construction, silhouette, material/color roles, anchor and apparent scale. Legitimate view-dependent widths do not require identical bounding boxes.
5. Record hidden construction as an explicit inference, its rationale and acceptance status, never a recovered fact. Repair conflicts through imagegen with identity and relevant accepted views within the shared caps. No manual painted fixes, code-drawn replacements or identity redefinition to excuse drift.
6. Before completed-set acceptance, follow the independent checkpoint policy in `references/visual-review.md`; keep individual creator reviews and bounded repairs. Accept each angle and the set separately under user approval or quoted delegation, preserving the actual actor, scope and exact hashes. Never claim the user approved unseen art. Missing requested angles, unresolved identity conflicts or exhausted repairs leave `needs_revision`/incomplete. Technical canvas/palette checks do not certify visual consistency.

## Deliver

Provide requested views, identity reference, source/native paths and hashes, integer previews and the compact record: view convention, dimensions, anchor/palette, inferred details, technical/visual findings, approvals and remaining budget. Reference-view acceptance does not automatically create accepted `native_master` assets. Only the full/continuation path adds a self-contained bundle and copied-bundle check.

Route to `action-pose-design` for action or `refine-pixel-art` for native refinement of a chosen view/set. Do not require unrequested angles or add views after budget exhaustion.
